{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-year-pm-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.69, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-year-pm`: `scale-county-timeagg-year`'s months (January, April, July and October 2020), day types, hours and road types with `<aggregateBy key=\"Year\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Year\"/>`, over the same county database (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`), for the gasoline passenger car (21) and the diesel combination long-haul truck (62), selecting the RUNNING-EXHAUST PM SPECIES: PM10 and PM2.5 total (100, 110), organic and elemental carbon (111, 112), sulfate (115), non-EC PM (118) and aerosol water (119). MOVESOutput is 5,390 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is SulfatePMCalculator and the PM chain (PM2.5 from EC and non-EC PM, OC from non-EC PM, PM10 from PM2.5) over PreAggYEAR.sql's collapsed FuelSupply, whose market shares SUM to 0.334 of the year over four months (§7.3.65, F63): the sulfate and water species read the supplied fuel's sulfur level through the formulations' shares, and `generalFuelRatio` scales EC and non-EC PM per formulation. It reproduced with no model change (PLAN.md §7.3.69): every species is a share-weighted mean the `ffsup_normalizer` port already normalises.\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1; `db_aggregationmonth` and `db_rateday` are read from its XML by `tools/runspec-month-selection.py` and `tools/runspec-day-selection.py`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 5390, the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs of the one (county, month, day) cell; `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "time-aggregation",
      "output-time-step",
      "year-aggregation",
      "pm-exhaust",
      "sulfate-pm"
    ]
  },
